    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78020.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "Well, I am way in favor of $15 minimum wage. I think the problem, and you know this, the problem is that you've got all these rules on, that's my puppy, I'm sorry. We got all these rules on what's the reality of what can go in a reconciliation package that only needs the 50 plus one vote. to pass. And so I wasn't for changing the rules to jam minimum wage in there. I'd love to see a consensus on minimum wage. So, number one, for people in leadership to send a message to working people in this country. that you're valued, you're valued at least at $32,000 a year. You know, one of the challenges I think that we have with the minimum wage is we talk about $15 an hour and everybody thinks, so when I was a kid, I only made two or three or whatever. And I just want to say, so someone right now, the minimum wage right now for someone working 40 hours a week is just a little bit over $15,000. I'd love to see anyone do the math on whether, in fact, we could, anyone, a family could survive on working full-time on where we are right now. Even if you move it to 15, it's just north of $30,000 a year. Even in the poorest of states with the cheapest living conditions, you can't make it working full-time on $32,000 a year, you just can't.",
