    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "I think that the House You know, the way I always explain this when people say, what do you think? I say, the house basically had enough to indict the president. They had enough information. And this isn't a criminal procedure, but I think the analogy holds. It was the Senate's job to try them. And if I have a criticism, I think they should have called witnesses. I think they should have put it front row and center, not just had the yak yak and the videos. I understand the videos had huge impact. But what would have been the impact if they had called a number of the DC officers, even if you guys didn't want to testify, but the DC officers, what would have been the impact if they had actually subpoenaed some of the people who were organizing?",
