  {
    "episode_id": 78020,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78020.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "Wow, that's a really, really good answer. One of the other questions that I have is even if it feels like even when the Democrats do pass something like this COVID bill, which is a good thing and no Republicans voted for it, it feels like they don't capitalize on that message that, hey, even though you're in hurting and you need the stimulus, we are the only ones that voted for it. I mean, I guess, at least I've framed this. Is there a way that the Democrats can become more aggressive without looking, like you said, they already have this arrogant feel to them, I guess, in some circles, but is there a way to champion what they're doing without coming off as, you know, like the elitist that I think a lot of people look at them as, you know, kind of now?",
