    "turn_text": "sides of the court. And so the first thing that I would say is they should be playing offense on what they just did and a values comparison on COVID, really, and the policies of the Republican Party. And then they need to turn to those things that put people back to work, that give people a sense of optimism and I would say that's infrastructure. And I think that's where Biden's going to go next. I think it's where the folks are going to go next and there'll be a lot of pearl clashing. Oh, the deficit. of that happened when they passed $1.9 trillion of tax rate. And so I am concerned long-term about debt deficit, but not if it's invested in infrastructure that we need to do anyway. And so I would say, find those things like this COVID relief package that are very popular. with the public, which I think infrastructure is, but you've got to message it. You've got to tell people what you're doing and why your values and why your government spending is so much better than what was been done in the past so that people understand that there's a choice here between people who will invest in human beings and invest in the services that people need and people who will just simply say, hand it to the millionaires and hope it trickles down.",
