    "turn_idx": 48,
    "turn_text": "Well, I don't want to belabor you guys either, but one of the things that I've been talking about. You mentioned that I was the attorney general in North Dakota, and I ran a law enforcement agency, and so still some of my best pals in North Dakota are the people that I work with in law enforcement. And so I understand how difficult that is. And I understand, I mean, I just, I watch that. And I have to tell you, Not only did I think about you guys, but I thought about your wives and your husband sitting home watching it and worried. And so, you know, people don't don't understand that. I think, I think if you haven't, if you haven't been in that world, I think they don't realize how hurtful it can be when they say things like, well, if this were Black Lives Matter, I would have been scared. And what Donald Trump did that will be his lasting legacy and it will be a lasting burden on the Republican Party, is he invited in to the tent, into the governing tent, white supremacist groups, you know, you know, the old keepers, the proud boys. I don't include the crazy Q people, even though I think they could be violent. I think they're just crazy. But, you know, when you think about these white supremacy groups, and that they've never been invited and given political power. And Donald Trump gave them political power.",
