    "turn_text": "is the end result. And how do we drive that force back now that they've had that power? And I think that's going to be a challenge for the Republican Party. And when you said, well, is this going to be challenged again? These were paramilitary groups that were very interested in being the militia for Donald Trump, not for the country, but for Donald Trump, because they see him as somebody who all of a sudden gave legitimacy to their anti-American and racist beliefs. And so, you know, they've got some healing to do over in the Republican Party, but I will tell you that the vast majority of people in this country look at all of you and watched and horror for all of you and for your families. But they also look at all of you as heroes. And I said, when I was on ABC, they said, well, the Capitol Police, because there was a lot of criticism, remember, when it was happening, because people were coming in and looked like they were on an impeded. And I said, wait a minute. The Capitol Police are defending and protecting the members. right now. They're not going to worry about who's in the rotunda unless there's a member in the rotunda. So just cut them some slack. They're overrun here. And I think that when you see and you see the videos and you see the bravery I'm reminded of the time I told a friend of mine, Mark, and you guys know Mark, too. He's retired since then, and he was talking about, you know, when you go through the screenings and people not taking that screening seriously, I said, you know, the Capitol Police guard the most significant image of America's democracy. And they do it every day with pride. And I watched as you guys have had to hand puff the people in wheelchairs when they were protesting the repeal of the ACA because they, you know, that was your job. I don't know that there is a tougher job in law enforcement than what you guys do, because it is so important to the country, but it is so important to achieve that balance between First Amendment and the right to express yourself and the protection of this cathedral of our democracy. And I just am so proud of all the friendships that I have within the Capitol, please. And just want to, again, on behalf of myself, my family, and I hope the people of North Dakota, thank you for your bravery. Thank you for everything that you do for our country.",
